<section id="data" aria-labelledby="h-board">
  <h2 id="h-board" class="sec">Leaderboard</h2>
  <p class="sub">Every logged run, next to the paper's models. Click a column to sort.</p>
  <div class="scroll" id="board-scroll"><table id="board"><tbody><tr class="skrow"><td><div class="sk"></div></td></tr><tr class="skrow"><td><div class="sk"></div></td></tr><tr class="skrow"><td><div class="sk"></div></td></tr><tr class="skrow"><td><div class="sk"></div></td></tr><tr class="skrow"><td><div class="sk"></div></td></tr><tr class="skrow"><td><div class="sk"></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <div class="tools">
    <details class="tool" id="filters-wrap"><summary>Filter runs</summary>
      <div class="filters" id="filters">
        <label>Runner <select id="f-runner"></select></label>
        <label>Split <select id="f-split"></select></label>
        <label>Action source <select id="f-action"></select></label>
        <label>Branch <select id="f-branch"></select></label>
        <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="f-tests"> Show pipeline tests <span id="hidden-count" class="std"></span></label>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="tool" id="compare"><summary>Compare to a baseline</summary>
      <p class="callout" style="margin-top:0">Per-family deltas against any run or paper model. Deltas under 2x the pass-to-pass std are labelled noise (same rule as <code>pwa compare</code>; the overall std is used for every family, or the paper's 0.105 when missing).</p>
      <div class="filters"><label>Baseline <select id="cmp-base"></select></label></div>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="cmp"></table></div>
      <p class="callout" id="cmp-note"></p>
    </details>
    <details class="tool"><summary>How to read this table</summary>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>Empty cells mean not measured, not zero.</li>
        <li>The best value in each score column is underlined. Only rows that pass every protocol check compare fairly with the paper rows.</li>
        <li>The filters also drive the charts in Progress.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cklegend" id="cklegend"></div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
